<title>CANADA: Canadian West Coast Vessel Loadings - CWB.</title>
<headline>Canadian West Coast Vessel Loadings - CWB.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Wheat Board reported six vessels loading, three waiting and seven due at the Canadian West Coast, as of Tuesday.</p>
<p>The longest vessel waiting to load in Vancouver waited five days. One ship was due in Churchill with two more expected next week. Three vessels loaded in Thunder Bay with seven more due. One ship loaded in Baie Comeau, Que., while six other ships waited on Canada's East Coast.</p>
<p>    Port	 Loading	Waiting</p>
<p>    Vancouver	6		 3</p>
<p>    Prince Rupert  0		 0</p>
<p>(Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548)</p>
